From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noxwell <beebono@yahoo.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 22:20:20 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 207/225] cpufreq: sprd: port realme 5.4-generation hwdvfs
 stack, retire old engine

The old 4.14-generation engine (sprd-cpufreqhw + our sprd-hwdvfs-normal)
resolves the DCDC_CPU1 voltage grade but never fires the autonomous I2C
transaction to the FAN53555, leaving the A75 cluster parked at 26 MHz.
Every software-settable TOP-DVFS register matches a working stock Android
on the same board, so port the driver generation stock actually runs
(realme sprd-hwdvfs-normal/-ums512/-cpufreq/-debugfs/-public), which
carries the DIALOG/I2C set path proven on this silicon.

- engine+archdata: sprd-hwdvfs-normal.c/ums512.c (tables in archdata,
  not DT); dvfs-blk-sd-syscon made optional (asserting BLOCK_SHUTDOWN
  with a dead CPU1 rail wedges the A75 cores and hangs boot)
- policy: sprd-hwdvfs-cpufreq.c + debugfs + public bridge (old-driver
  branch trimmed); topology_cluster_id() for post-5.16 cpu-map semantics
- 5.4->7.1 API: void .exit/.remove, dev_pm_opp_of_register_em(dev, ..),
  1-arg i2c probe, no CPUFREQ_STICKY/.attr, cpufreq_cpu_get in public
- Kconfig/Makefile/defconfig: ARM_SPRD_HW_CPUFREQ_NORMAL/_ARCH_UMS512/
  _PUBLIC + ARM_SPRD_TOP_DVFS (sprd-top-dvfs.c kept), drop
  ARM_SPRD_CPUFREQ_HW and its files
- DT: realme-gen bindings - opp-table0/1 policy nodes (base T618
  operating-points, no bin/multi-version), dvfs-dcdc-cpuX-cfg supply
  cfgs, dcdc-cpuX reduced to dcdc-cpu-dvfs-cfg phandles,
  sprd,topdvfs-sysctrl self-ref, hardware-dvfs-platform bind node,
  cpudvfs-dev rewritten to host/slave-cluster-cells + archdata tables

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
